WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.000
{IF YOU ARE SEEING THIS, YOUR PLAYER IS NOT RENDERING THE SUBTITLES PROPERLY. PLEASE REFER TO http://saizen-fansubs.com/?section=playback FOR THE INTENDED PLAYBACK.}

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.110
We will now have you do the final test.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:07.830
In this test...

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:10.400
we will have you play as a team.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.360
Team?

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.030
Your opponents are...

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:17.200
Our Salmons'...

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.780
Single A team:

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.240
The Tucson Red Rox.

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:24.160
Look at that!

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:35.310
There is only one condition you must clear to pass the test...

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:37.810
You have to come back and defeat the Red Rox.

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:43.010
Nice batting!

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:44.730
Just what you'd expect from our helper!

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.790
Follow it up, Shigeno!

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:47.660
Leave it to me!

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.290
<i>Top of the third inning...</i>

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:53.960
<i>Ten run difference, no outs, a runner on first base...</i>

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:58.120
<i>In this situation, rather than aiming for a big one and trying to score two runs,</i>

00:00:58.850 --> 00:00:59.880
<i>I need to hit it to the outfield...</i>

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:03.250
<i>to help the runner proceed!</i>

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.290
It went through!

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:10.710
All right!

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:13.840
It seems like...

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:18.300
out of all of them, he understands the meaning of this test best.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.390
Yeah.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:56.570
He looks happy!

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.330
That was great!

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:58.820
You did great!

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.540
Nice batting!

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.590
I love you!

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:04.030
He sure is carefree.

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:05.460
Show off.

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:10.850
We're counting on you, Ginumacchi!

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:12.090
Keep it going!

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:13.640
<i>It's the top of the third inning.</i>

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:14.800
<i>We're still behind by ten runs.</i>

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.540
<i>We have no outs and runners on first and third base.</i>

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:18.770
<i>I don't need a big one.</i>

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:21.440
<i>What I should do is carry it through to the back of the order.</i>

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:26.570
<i>Don't get big headed just because you got a couple of hits!</i>

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:32.910
It's fair!

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:37.370
Keep going around!

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:45.790
Safe!

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:46.740
He did it!

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.250
Nice run, Goro!

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:52.130
Let's keep it going, Aguilera!

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:53.590
Let's keep it going!

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:54.420
All right!

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:55.570
We're counting on you!

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:55.570
Keep it going!

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:56.680
Keep it going!

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:59.260
<i>We're going to win this no matter what!</i>

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:01.640
<i>We'll win this and pass!</i>

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:07.440
Ball!

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:08.460
Ball four!

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:10.190
All right!

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:12.920
That was great, number two-kun!

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:16.520
It's Nick now, and we have no outs with runners on first and second.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:18.490
It's the same situation as the first inning.

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:19.160
Hey!

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:22.470
I won't forgive you if you mess up again!

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:33.260
<i>Do you think the same pitch is going to work on me again!?</i>

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:37.850
Out!

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:39.600
Out!

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:41.790
Damn it!

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:43.310
A failed hit.

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:47.020
<i>Damn.</i>

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:54.990
<i>So we were stopped and only scored three runs.</i>

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.710
<i>That bastard.</i>

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:01.760
Play!

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:06.790
<i>Well, I'll just defend this inning and attack again!</i>

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:13.780
All right, Andy!

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.030
That's one hit!

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:16.970
Like we're going to let it end like this!

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:18.520
Sorry, sorry!

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:20.860
My hand just slipped.

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:22.120
Don't worry about it.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.750
Let's just hold the next one back.

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:34.610
Ball!

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:44.500
Ball!

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:45.690
Ball four!

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:51.910
<i>What's the matter, Shigeno?</i>

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.170
<i>Shit.</i>

00:05:58.300 --> 00:05:59.260
Ball!

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:02.350
Ball!

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:05.350
<i>Shit!</i>

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:08.100
<i>My blister just burst.</i>

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:10.980
<i>I thought I was prepared,</i>

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:16.770
<i>but because I took so much time rehabbing my leg, it looks like I didn't spend enough time throwing.</i>

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:19.130
Umpire, time!

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:22.410
Shortstop, translate!

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:31.710
"Stop showing off and trying to strike out the side when you can't even get strikes."

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:34.780
"This isn't just your test."

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:35.630
That's what he says.

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:40.090
Just quietly throw it down the middle.

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:41.800
Understand?

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:46.340
Don't worry about it, Goro.

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:48.460
Just let him talk.

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:50.470
Shigeno, just loosen up a bit.

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:55.130
Play!

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.850
<i>This isn't just my test, huh?</i>

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:01.820
<i>He's right.</i>

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:06.780
<i>I wasn't thinking straight and got carried away because of a mere blister bursting.</i>

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:10.840
<i>In that case, I'll just let them hit and rely on them fielding it!</i>

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:14.400
<i>I'm counting on you all!</i>

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:19.220
Out!

00:07:19.220 --> 00:07:21.180
Nice, Ginumacchi!

00:07:23.510 --> 00:07:24.450
<i>That guy.</i>

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:27.290
<i>Why is he happy over someone else's fine play?</i>

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:29.600
<i>Yaginuma!</i>

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:31.500
<i>What did he say just now?</i>

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.740
<i>He said something about the Majors, right?</i>

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:34.800
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:38.240
<i>He said that if we can't score ten runs and defeat a Single A team,</i>

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:43.190
<i>we won't have a chance at reaching the Major League.</i>

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:45.780
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:50.330
<i>he's really thinking of winning this game and...</i>

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:58.710
Out!

00:07:58.710 --> 00:07:59.590
All right!

00:07:59.590 --> 00:08:01.720
All right! Nice, Chris!

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:02.680
Yeah!

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:11.930
<i>Oh no!</i>

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:15.110
All right!

00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:15.770
It's going to get through!

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:23.980
Bartheg!

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:30.250
Out!

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:36.040
You've got to be kidding me.

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:39.850
Nice effort, Bartheg!

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:41.060
Are you all right?

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:41.840
Yeah.

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:43.220
That was great! Just great!

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:44.210
Thank you!

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:45.530
You're the best!

00:08:45.530 --> 00:08:46.360
No!

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:48.550
Stop it, Goro!

00:08:48.550 --> 00:08:50.140
You're the best! The best!

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.970
I get it. I get it.

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:51.970
The best! The best!

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:53.870
I'm going to kiss you!

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:55.440
Hey!

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:56.790
Just keep this up!

00:08:56.790 --> 00:08:58.610
I'm going to kiss you!

00:09:09.910 --> 00:09:10.700
Safe!

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:18.920
<i>It's his turn again when we have a chance!</i>

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:19.740
Nick!

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:21.260
Keep it going this time!

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:24.340
<i>Shut up.</i>

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:29.140
<i>I don't have to be told by a colored!</i>

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:33.770
He went for a sacrifice bunt!?

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:36.520
To first!

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:38.270
Out!

00:09:57.440 --> 00:09:59.420
Nice bunt!

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:04.840
It's not like I'm doing this for the coloreds.

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:06.880
I caught that!

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:07.530
Hey!

00:10:07.530 --> 00:10:10.800
You said something about colors again, didn't you!?

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:10.800
Hey!

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:16.160
It looks like the others have started to realize.

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:16.950
Yeah.

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:23.150
Even if it's from 10-0, those who really believe they can turn the tables around,

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:29.610
and those who have the power to turn their situation around, however bad it is, through their hard work and courage...

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:30.790
All right!

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:33.650
It's only those with tough mental power that have the right...

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:32.440
Go for it!

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:35.030
Don't waste this chance!

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:37.540
to challenge the sharp thorns on the road to the Majors.

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:36.220
Keep it going!

00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:37.540
Follow him, Chris!

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:39.280
Play!

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:43.980
<i>Nick went to the trouble of sacrificing himself.</i>

00:10:43.980 --> 00:10:46.960
<i>Whatever it takes, I have to get the runners...</i>

00:10:47.590 --> 00:10:48.490
<i>around!</i>

00:10:50.510 --> 00:10:55.540
This is a free fansub.

00:10:50.510 --> 00:10:55.540
Not for sale or rent.

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:58.400
Right field!

00:10:59.060 --> 00:10:59.910
All right!

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:01.650
It's an easy sacrifice fly!

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:18.130
All right!

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:18.130
We did it!

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:21.000
We're now one run behind!

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:23.890
I knew you'd be able to do it!

00:11:23.890 --> 00:11:25.430
Nice homerun!

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:29.180
What?

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:32.760
There wasn't a point in me sacrificing myself if you could hit a homerun.

00:11:33.430 --> 00:11:35.100
No.

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:40.770
It went well because I was able to think it was all right to hit a sacrifice fly.

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:43.420
Thank you for sacrificing yourself, Nick.

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:02.210
So we've come to the last inning just one run behind.

00:12:02.210 --> 00:12:03.310
Damn it!

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:05.320
We can't score that one run!

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:09.470
We were able to corner them this far, but we need to catch up to them in this last inning at least.

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:11.610
I wonder if we still can't pass.

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:23.700
<i>After they changed to that southpaw with irregular pitches,
we've only gotten runners from walks and one hit from Robbins.</i>

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:25.880
<i>Please, Shigeno.</i>

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:28.070
<i>Get to first base somehow!</i>

00:12:28.070 --> 00:12:28.770
Play!

00:12:35.910 --> 00:12:37.280
Did it go!?

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:42.450
Out!

00:12:43.750 --> 00:12:45.170
Shit!

00:12:45.850 --> 00:12:48.090
My aim was off!

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:52.410
We're counting on you, Yaginuma!

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:54.470
Let's get out on the bases somehow!

00:12:56.570 --> 00:13:00.100
<i>I'm not good with pitchers that have different pitches like him.</i>

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:02.770
Ball!

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:06.240
<i>But I have to...</i>

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:07.690
<i>I have to get on base somehow.</i>

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:12.030
Ball two!

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:14.140
<i>All right! I can walk!</i>

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:15.950
<i>My chances are higher than trying to hit it!</i>

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:20.250
Strike!

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:21.150
<i>Damn!</i>

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:22.330
<i>He went for the middle.</i>

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:26.290
Strike!

00:13:28.360 --> 00:13:30.140
<i>Those last two pitches were easy.</i>

00:13:30.140 --> 00:13:31.510
<i>Should I have gone for them!?</i>

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:33.130
What are you doing, Ginumacchi!

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:35.950
This is your last chance!

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:38.720
What's the point if you don't show off your batting skills!?

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:41.170
This isn't the only test there is!

00:13:41.170 --> 00:13:43.140
Stop being scared and hit!

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:44.090
<i>T-That's right.</i>

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:45.490
<i>T-That's right.</i>

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:48.310
<i>I was like this with all the tryouts I've taken so far.</i>

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:51.270
<i>Even if I was able to pass the physical test,</i>

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:58.700
<i>when it came to the real game test, I always got nervous and made terrible mistakes, hitting easy grounders.</i>

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:00.660
<i>What am I doing!?</i>

00:14:00.660 --> 00:14:02.620
<i>Without having confidence in my own strength...</i>

00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:07.710
<i>How can I grasp my dreams in America if I'm like that!?</i>

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:12.630
All right!

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:15.340
All right! We now have a runner!

00:14:15.340 --> 00:14:17.060
Follow him, Aguilera!

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:18.090
We're counting on you!

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.510
All right! Let's go!

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:28.190
Strike out!

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:30.100
T-Two out.

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:31.150
T-Two out.

00:14:32.270 --> 00:14:32.720
I-I'm sorry.

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:33.880
I-I'm sorry.

00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:35.320
Please do something.

00:14:36.110 --> 00:14:36.990
Play!

00:14:39.950 --> 00:14:41.440
Hit it!

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:43.620
We're all going to fail if you don't hit it!

00:14:47.100 --> 00:14:48.460
Strike!

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:58.760
<i>For a long time, my old man had a habit and said,</i>

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:02.910
<i>"There isn't a colored that's any good."</i>

00:15:04.270 --> 00:15:07.850
<i>And, "Don't believe in colored people." </i>

00:15:11.280 --> 00:15:12.240
Ball!

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:20.050
<i>In reality, there were horrible people around me.</i>

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:31.250
<i>But...</i>

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:34.040
<i>even if that was reality,</i>

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:36.170
<i>it's not the truth!</i>

00:15:36.170 --> 00:15:41.590
<i>At least those guys over there aren't the coloreds I knew of and imagined.</i>

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:46.060
<i>They all have eyes like mine, dreaming of the Majors.</i>

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:49.060
<i>And their eyes believe in it without hesitation!</i>

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:58.290
<i>I was just discriminating against them because of their skin color, believing in my old man's words.</i>

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:03.110
Do you have a spare bat, Nick?

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:05.390
N-No.

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:06.030
N-No.

00:16:06.640 --> 00:16:09.990
Then use my bat if you like.

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:12.000
It's the bat I hit a homerun with today.

00:16:12.510 --> 00:16:13.940
Its luck isn't that bad.

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:23.720
Thank you.

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:36.730
<i>We will pass!</i>

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:41.190
<i>When we're on the field, it doesn't matter if we're white, black, or yellow!</i>

00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:48.330
<i>We just hit our spirit into the white ball, going beyond all language barriers and borders!</i>

00:16:56.480 --> 00:16:57.710
He did it!

00:16:57.710 --> 00:16:58.590
All right!

00:17:02.730 --> 00:17:04.720
Slide in, Ginumacchi!

00:17:20.920 --> 00:17:21.650
O-Out!

00:17:21.650 --> 00:17:23.280
O-Out!

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:31.580
Damn it!

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:37.800
W-We lost...

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:38.670
W-We lost...

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:47.190
I-I'm sorry.

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:48.050
I-I'm sorry.

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:49.770
Don't worry about it.

00:17:49.770 --> 00:17:51.140
We all did well.

00:17:51.140 --> 00:17:52.670
It was a nice game.

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:54.520
"Nice"!?

00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:57.420
There's no point if we lost!

00:17:57.420 --> 00:18:01.400
We all failed this tryout when we were just a step away!

00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:08.300
Congratulations.

00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:13.620
You guys weren't able to reverse the scores but did enough.

00:18:13.620 --> 00:18:16.330
You all pass the tryout.

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:20.550
W-What was that?

00:18:20.550 --> 00:18:22.210
W-What was that?

00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:24.600
He said we all passed.

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:25.280
W-What!?

00:18:25.280 --> 00:18:26.900
W-What!?

00:18:26.900 --> 00:18:30.010
Was the talk of failing if we didn't win all a lie!?

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:32.770
The Major League is a pro sport.

00:18:32.770 --> 00:18:36.750
Therefore, you may think that skill and ability are the most important things, and are valued above anything else.

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:38.440
But that's not it.

00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:40.750
A good personality...

00:18:40.750 --> 00:18:41.810
In other words, teamwork, trust, courtesy, passion, ambition.

00:18:41.810 --> 00:18:42.810
