Unless you have all these, even if you have the skills, you will never be a true Major Leaguer.

00:18:57.550 --> 00:19:01.540
You have to be someone admired by the people, and someone who could give them a dream.

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:06.130
You won't reach it unless you're that person.

00:19:06.850 --> 00:19:11.340
But today you've all shown us that you have that gift.

00:19:12.040 --> 00:19:15.220
You'll all probably start from the Rookie League,

00:19:15.220 --> 00:19:19.770
but if you have the will to aim for the Majors with the Salmons, go sign the contract.

00:19:25.570 --> 00:19:27.510
We did it!

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:29.950
We did it!

00:19:33.050 --> 00:19:34.100
We really did it!

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:35.120
Yeah.

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:39.480
Spring training has already begun.

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:43.290
After signing the contract, those who have to sort out their visas,

00:19:43.290 --> 00:19:50.720
please finish that as soon as possible, and then join the Minors group to start your new lives.

00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:52.800
Oh, however,

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:54.690
there's an exception for one of you.

00:19:56.220 --> 00:19:57.660
Goro Shigeno.

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:03.420
You'll be joining the Majors group on the main field next door.

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:09.890
What did he say?

00:20:11.330 --> 00:20:14.130
He said you're going to the Majors camp!

00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:19.250
They're already giving you the chance to tryout for the Major League roster!

00:20:19.250 --> 00:20:20.500
W-WHAT!?

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:23.260
W-WHAT!?

00:20:28.780 --> 00:20:30.170
I see.

00:20:30.170 --> 00:20:32.740
So you're going to return to Japan for now.

00:20:33.530 --> 00:20:35.470
Well, I have a lot of things to sort out.

00:20:36.110 --> 00:20:38.640
And I also need to convince my parents.

00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:41.550
Make sure to call your parents too, okay?

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:42.950
I forgot.

00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:44.770
Shigeno.

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:49.860
Are you really okay with joining the Salmons?

00:20:49.860 --> 00:20:51.290
Huh?

00:20:51.290 --> 00:20:52.820
What's that supposed to mean?

00:20:52.820 --> 00:20:54.390
No.

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:58.940
It's just that with your skills, you could probably pass other tryouts.

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:02.800
The Salmons are a renowned team, but they've been stuck as a second tier team the last couple of years.

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:05.750
They don't have the strength to challenge for the World Series.

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:09.590
Maybe you don't have to rush and sign up with them.

00:21:10.920 --> 00:21:14.620
It's not like I know much about the other teams, so it doesn't matter where I join.

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:16.420
They've been a second tier team the last couple of years?

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:17.930
No problem.

00:21:18.620 --> 00:21:23.350
In that case, it just means I'll make the Salmons world champions with my own hands.

00:21:25.310 --> 00:21:27.240
Just joking.

00:21:27.240 --> 00:21:31.630
A guy like me, whose pitch was easily hit by Bolton, has no time to be showing off.

00:21:32.930 --> 00:21:36.790
Well, that's something to talk about after I get on the toaster.

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:38.990
You mean the "roster"...

00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:44.790
Ginumacchi.

00:21:44.790 --> 00:21:47.540
Contact me again when you come back to America.

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:50.000
That talk we had earlier.

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:52.840
In the final game that decides the world champions,

00:21:52.840 --> 00:21:57.220
the shortstop that's going to be defending the mound behind me is...

00:21:57.220 --> 00:21:59.260
going to be Yaginuma Hayato.

00:22:04.160 --> 00:22:05.480
Yeah.

00:22:12.470 --> 00:22:15.340
<i>Twenty-five roster spots, huh?</i>

00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:18.110
<i>I'll survive it no matter what.</i>

00:22:18.590 --> 00:22:20.560
<i>Just you wait, Gibson.</i>

00:22:20.560 --> 00:22:25.680
<i>I'll get to the Majors soon- where you wait. </i>

00:22:29.960 --> 00:22:32.050
Oh, I forgot.

00:22:32.050 --> 00:22:35.490
About the money for the stay in the twin room and the meals I paid for you.

00:22:35.490 --> 00:22:37.570
When you get the money, just pay it into this account.

00:22:37.570 --> 00:22:38.720
You're joking!

00:24:11.290 --> 00:24:12.810
I did it!

00:24:12.810 --> 00:24:16.610
I'm suddenly allowed to go to the Majors camp!

00:24:16.610 --> 00:24:19.440
I bet there are a lot of incredible players!

00:24:19.440 --> 00:24:22.150
All right! I'm so excited!

00:24:22.150 --> 00:24:23.230
Next time, on Major:

00:24:23.230 --> 00:24:24.910
This is the Majors!

00:24:24.910 --> 00:24:27.420
Run to the stage of your dreams!
